# Starter ship blueprint — AUTHORED 1×, upscaled ×world_scale at boot
# (2026-08-31, retiring the native-8× experiment). EDIT ME — the game
# loads this file and `ShipLayout.upscale_cells` grows it to the world's
# scale with true component footprints (engine 4×4, door 1×8, propeller
# 6×2/2×6, helm 4×7, turret 2×8 — BlockDB.FOOTPRINT_8X), exactly like
# every Blueprint Loft ship. That makes this file LOFT-NATIVE: export,
# edit, paste it back.
#
# WHY THE NATIVE-8× FILE RETIRED (owner: "impossible to move sideways"):
# hand-authoring at 8× granularity gave the hull 64× the bulk mass while
# its components only carried their footprint RATINGS — measured, the
# ship peaked at 94 px/s laterally: one wind-ring tile in 12 minutes.
# The upscaler exists precisely to keep an authored ship's FEEL at any
# scale (pinned by _test_scale_unit_preserves_feel); authored 1× and
# upscaled, the same silhouette flies with the authority the mode's
# weather was tuned against.
#
# One character per block:
#   .  empty        #  hull         G  gasbag (lift, free)
#   E  engine       H  helm         B  ballast
#   W  blubber      D  door (spawns closed; F opens/closes)
#   -  platform (S+jump drops through)
#   ^ v < > P V  propeller — ONE component, axis comes from mounting:
#                 side neighbour = horizontal, above/below = vertical
#
# Layout is the same vessel as ever: gasbag canopy; two cabins with
# doors and the helm indoors; deck hatches dropping into the machine
# hold (six engines, protected inside, the hatch landing kept clear)
# and out the belly;
# pushers at bow AND stern PLUS a low pair port and starboard (the
# 2026-08-31 upgrade — four horizontal pushers and six engines, so the
# hull can actually cross the wind ring and never brown-outs at full
# burn); lift props hung beneath; turrets slung from the hull (the last
# strut retired 2026-09-01 with the type's exit from the palette).
#
# 'origin COL ROW' names which character is ship cell (0,0).

# HEADERS (2026-09-05) — what this file already was, said out loud, so the
# drafting table can file it. Header lines only: the grid below is untouched.
name Starter
kind vessel

origin 6 5

GGGGGGGGGGGG
GGGGGGGGGGGG
